 If the query result changes so the function would return a positive number again, polling resumes automatically."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"background-polling","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Background polling"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, polling pauses when the browser tab loses focus. For dashboards or any interface where data needs to stay current even while the user is in another tab, disable that behavior:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"useQuery(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['portfolio'],\n  queryFn: fetchPortfolio,\n  refetchInterval: 30_000,\n  refetchIntervalInBackground: true,\n}))","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"pausing-polling","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pausing polling"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass a function to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"refetchInterval"},{"type":"text","value":" and close over component state to control when polling runs:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"useQuery(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['prices', tokenAddress],\n  queryFn: () => fetchPrice(tokenAddress),\n  refetchInterval: () => {\n    if (!tokenAddress || isPaused) return false\n    return 15_000\n  },\n}))","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"polling-with-offline-support","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Polling with offline support"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Query detects connectivity by listening to the browser's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"online"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"offline"},{"type":"text","value":" events. In environments where those events don't fire reliably (Electron, some embedded WebViews), set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"networkMode: 'always'"},{"type":"text","value":" to skip the connectivity check:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"useQuery(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['chainStatus'],\n  queryFn: fetchChainStatus,\n  refetchInterval: 10_000,\n  networkMode: 'always',\n}))","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For more on network modes, see "},{"type":"link","href":"./network-mode.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Network Mode"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"note-on-deduplication","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note on deduplication"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryObserver"},{"type":"text","value":" (each component using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQuery"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"refetchInterval"},{"type":"text","value":") runs its own timer. Two components subscribed to the same key with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"refetchInterval: 5000"},{"type":"text","value":" each fire their timer every 5 seconds. What gets deduplicated is concurrent in-flight fetches: if two timers fire at the same time, only one network request goes out. The timers are observer-level; the deduplication is query-level."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"adapting-the-interval-to-query-state","text":"Adapting the interval to query state","level":2},{"id":"background-polling","text":"Background polling","level":2},{"id":"pausing-polling","text":"Pausing polling","level":2},{"id":"polling-with-offline-support","text":"Polling with offline support","level":2},{"id":"note-on-deduplication","text":"Note on deduplication","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n`refetchInterval` makes a query refetch on a timer. Set it to a number in milliseconds and the query runs every N ms while there's at least one active observer:\n\n\n\n```tsx\nuseQuery(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['prices'],\n  queryFn: fetchPrices,\n  refetchInterval: 5_000, // every 5 seconds\n}))\n```\n\n\n\nPolling is independent of `staleTime`. A query can be fresh and still poll on schedule; see [Important Defaults](./important-defaults.md) for how `staleTime` interacts with other refetch behaviors. `refetchInterval` fires on its own clock regardless of freshness.\n\n## Adapting the interval to query state\n\nPass a function instead of a number to compute the interval from the current query. The function receives the `Query` object and should return a number in ms or `false` to stop polling:\n\n\n\n```tsx\nuseQuery(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['job', jobId],\n  queryFn: () => fetchJobStatus(jobId),\n  refetchInterval: (query) => {\n    // Stop polling once the job finishes\n    if (query.state.data?.status === 'complete') return false\n    return 2_000\n  },\n}))\n```\n\n\n\nReturning `false` clears the interval timer. If the query result changes so the function would return a positive number again, polling resumes automatically.\n\n## Background polling\n\nBy default, polling pauses when the browser tab loses focus. For dashboards or any interface where data needs to stay current even while the user is in another tab, disable that behavior:\n\n\n\n```tsx\nuseQuery(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['portfolio'],\n  queryFn: fetchPortfolio,\n  refetchInterval: 30_000,\n  refetchIntervalInBackground: true,\n}))\n```\n\n\n\n## Pausing polling\n\nPass a function to `refetchInterval` and close over component state to control when polling runs:\n\n\n\n```tsx\nuseQuery(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['prices', tokenAddress],\n  queryFn: () => fetchPrice(tokenAddress),\n  refetchInterval: () => {\n    if (!tokenAddress || isPaused) return false\n    return 15_000\n  },\n}))\n```\n\n\n\n## Polling with offline support\n\nTanStack Query detects connectivity by listening to the browser's `online` and `offline` events. In environments where those events don't fire reliably (Electron, some embedded WebViews), set `networkMode: 'always'` to skip the connectivity check:\n\n\n\n```tsx\nuseQuery(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['chainStatus'],\n  queryFn: fetchChainStatus,\n  refetchInterval: 10_000,\n  networkMode: 'always',\n}))\n```\n\n\n\nFor more on network modes, see [Network Mode](./network-mode.md).\n\n## Note on deduplication\n\nEach `QueryObserver` (each component using `useQuery` with `refetchInterval`) runs its own timer. Two components subscribed to the same key with `refetchInterval: 5000` each fire their timer every 5 seconds. What gets deduplicated is concurrent in-flight fetches: if two timers fire at the same time, only one network request goes out. The timers are observer-level; the deduplication is query-level.\n\n\n\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: polling\ntitle: Polling\nref: docs/framework/react/guides/polling.md\nreplace: { '@tanstack/react-query': '@tanstack/solid-query' }\n---\n\n[//]: # 'Example1'\n\n```tsx\nuseQuery(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['prices'],\n  queryFn: fetchPrices,\n  refetchInterval: 5_000, // every 5 seconds\n}))\n```\n\n[//]: # 'Example1'\n[//]: # 'Example2'\n\n```tsx\nuseQuery(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['job', jobId],\n  queryFn: () => fetchJobStatus(jobId),\n  refetchInterval: (query) => {\n    // Stop polling once the job finishes\n    if (query.state.data?.status === 'complete') return false\n    return 2_000\n  },\n}))\n```\n\n[//]: # 'Example2'\n[//]: # 'Example3'\n\n```tsx\nuseQuery(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['portfolio'],\n  queryFn: fetchPortfolio,\n  refetchInterval: 30_000,\n  refetchIntervalInBackground: true,\n}))\n```\n\n[//]: # 'Example3'\n[//]: # 'Example4'\n\n```tsx\nuseQuery(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['prices', tokenAddress],\n  queryFn: () => fetchPrice(tokenAddress),\n  refetchInterval: () => {\n    if (!tokenAddress || isPaused) return false\n    return 15_000\n  },\n}))\n```\n\n[//]: # 'Example4'\n[//]: # 'Example5'\n\n```tsx\nuseQuery(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['chainStatus'],\n  queryFn: fetchChainStatus,\n  refetchInterval: 10_000,\n  networkMode: 'always',\n}))\n```\n\n[//]: # 'Example5'\n[//]: # 'ReactNative'\n[//]: # 'ReactNative'\n"}
